        "h": "What this chapter compressed, and what is not here",
        "body": "### ⚠️ The split, recorded\n- **Printed at 17 pp:** `nr-lmn` was written whole against **both decks**, spliced and printed — **four pages past the ≤13 hard shape**.\n- **The seam:** the **DECK BOUNDARY**. **This chapter is `L6) Peripheral neuropathy`**; **`nr-lmn` is `L5) Muscle Disease`** and the neuromuscular junction.\n- **Why it is allowed:** **two topics**, not one topic taught over two lectures, so **CLAUDE.md §4's merge rule does not bind**.\n- **⚠️ It reverses a recorded merge:** the original **`nr-lmn1` + `nr-lmn2`** join at the head of `app\\data\\modules.js`. **SCHEDULE is untouched**, per §4 and the `nr-hemi`/`nr-para` precedent.\n- **⚠️ This chapter is NEW:** it did not exist before 2026-08-22.\n\n### ⚠️ Register (§14.5) — half of one received row is delivered here\n\n|**Owed by**|**Fact**|**Delivered**|\n|---|---|---|\n|**`nr-hemi`** *(hem-16)*|**PERIPHERAL NEUROPATHY** and **GUILLAIN-BARRÉ as diseases**|✅ **`pn-1`**-`pn-3` and **`pn-4`**|\n|**`nr-hemi`** *(hem-16)*|**NERVE CONDUCTION STUDIES and EMG** as techniques|✅ **`nr-lmn`**, section `lm-1`, where the framework they belong to is written|\n\n- **The rest of that row** — myasthenia gravis, muscular dystrophy and motor neuron disease — **is delivered in `nr-lmn`**, and the **UMN/LMN framework the other three rows name** is in **`lm-1`**. **Neither is repeated here.**\n- **No row is filed OUT of this chapter.**\n\n### ⚠️ One compression, recorded\n- **L6's Table (1):** 30 rows and four columns. **Every named cause and every laboratory test is kept** in `pn-2`. The **MANIFESTATION-CODE column** — S sensory, SM sensorimotor, M motor, SYM symmetric, MF multifocal, CN cranial nerve — **was dropped as a column**, and its content written as prose beneath the table. **No cause and no test is dropped.**\n\n### Deck quality — measured, not assumed\n- **The page audit:** **10 of L6's 44 pages carry fewer than 12 extractable words**.\n- **⚠️ The four zero-text pages carry ZERO FONTS** — p29, p31, p42 and p43 — checked with `pdffonts` page by page, **so no text is hidden as vector outlines**. All four are **genuine picture slides**, carrying **7, 8, 7 and 3 images**.\n- **⚠️ p1 is the title slide** and its single font is the **Arabic basmala**, which the cache preserves and this chapter does not use.\n- **Nothing was rendered.** The two figures that matter — the **diffuse mononuclear infiltrate in GBS** and **WALLERIAN DEGENERATION** — are **legended in the extracted text**, and the Wallerian legend is written out in full in `pn-4`.\n\n### What this deck does not contain\n- **⚠️ CMT:** named as the **commonest hereditary neuropathy** in two places and **NEVER DESCRIBED**. No clinical picture, no inheritance, no age of onset — its entire content is the **DNA test list** and the **demyelinating/axonal split** in `pn-2`.\n- **No treatment for diabetic neuropathy**, and **no drug named for neuropathic pain anywhere in the deck** — the phrase is *amelioration of pain*, with no agent behind it.\n- **⚠️ No dose, no schedule:** for the two GBS treatments. Plasmapheresis and IVIG are named as *early* and nothing more. *(The IVIG regimen in `nr-lmn`'s `lm-9`, 0.4 mg/kg/day for 5 days, is L5's and is for MYASTHENIA — it is not stated for GBS and is not transferred here.)*\n- **No CIDP**, and **no chronic demyelinating neuropathy** of any kind — GBS is the only immune neuropathy described.\n- **No prognosis figures for GBS** — the course is given in phases and never in percentages.\n\nSrc: L6 read end to end; the page audit is a `pdftotext` / `pdffonts` / `pdfimages` sweep of all 44 pages, 2026-08-22. The register rows are quoted from `hem-16` in app\\data\\theory.neuro.js on disk",
