        "h": "The split, the register, and what this deck does not contain",
        "body": "### ⚠️ The split, recorded\n- **Forecast, not found:** `theory-plan.md` §4 named this **the module's only forecast split**, and the old title admitted it — **\"Movement disorders / Epilepsy\"** are **two topics**, not one topic taught over two lectures, so **CLAUDE.md §4's merge rule never applied**.\n- **The seam:** the **deck boundary**. **`L3) MOVEMENT DISORDERS` here**; **`L4) Seizures_Epilepsy` in `nr-epilepsy`**.\n- **The arithmetic:** **2,699 + 2,321 = 5,020 source words**, forecast **15.0 pp at ÷335** and more on every smaller divisor — **past the ≤13 hard shape on all of them**.\n- **⚠️ Split BEFORE writing**, which is what the method asks where the evidence is already in hand: splitting after printing cost two extra cycles in ophthalmology, and two more in this module on 2026-08-22. **`SCHEDULE` untouched**; the single question stays here.\n\n### ⚠️ Register (§14.5)\n\n|**Owed by**|**Fact**|**Delivered**|\n|---|---|---|\n|**`nr-para`** *(hem-16)*|**EPILEPSY** as a disease, named in `hem-2` as a tempo cause of hemiplegia|✅ **`nr-epilepsy`** — the sibling half of this split|\n|**`nr-para`** *(hem-16)*|**TODD'S PARALYSIS**|✅ **`nr-epilepsy`** — L4 prints it twice, in the post-ictal state and in the syncope checklist|\n|**`nr-para`** *(hem-16)*|**MIGRAINE**|✅ already delivered by **`nr-headache`**|\n\n- **No row is filed OUT of this chapter.** Every disease named here is taught here.\n- **Not repeated:** the **five other gaits** of the match set are `hem-15`'s and `lm-3`'s; the **UMN/LMN framework** the red flags invoke is `nr-lmn`'s **`lm-1`**; **tics against compulsions** is `ps-ocd`'s **`oc-6`**.\n\n### ⚠️ Deck quality — and one page that could not be read\n- **The page audit:** **51 pages, six under 15 extractable words** — **p2** title art · **p7** the basal-ganglia figure · **p17** · **p18** the prompt slide · **p30** the HYPERKINETIC divider · **p51** the closing slide.\n- **⚠️⚠️ ONLY p17 HAS ZERO FONTS**, with two images, and it is the **one page in the deck whose content is unknown**. It sits **immediately before the `MOTOR / NON MOTOR / SYMPTOMS ??????` slide**, so on position it is **almost certainly an illustration rather than the answer** — **an inference, not a reading.** Rendering it needs a subagent, which was **not available in this session**. **Recorded, not guessed.**\n- **⚠️ Book Neuro ch.12, Movement Disorders — printed 119-127, nine pages — is UNREAD and uncached.** It is the other place the non-motor list may be printed. **`mv-5`'s supplied table is the first thing to check if either is ever read.**\n\n### What this deck does not contain\n- **⚠️ THE NON-MOTOR SYMPTOMS:** of Parkinson's disease. The deck **asks for them on a slide and never answers** — supplied and tagged in `mv-5`, and this is the largest fill in the chapter.\n- **⚠️ PSP and CBS:** **named only as ABBREVIATIONS** on the red-flag list. **No Parkinson-plus syndrome is described** — not progressive supranuclear palsy, not corticobasal syndrome, not multiple system atrophy, which is not named at all.\n- **⚠️ MYOCLONUS and STEREOTYPIES:** **named in `mv-1`'s hyperkinetic list and DESCRIBED NOWHERE.** Every other member of that list gets its own section.\n- **No dose for any drug** except **BIPERIDEN 2 mg tab**, and **no dose at all for levodopa, any agonist, rasagiline, entacapone, amantadine, haloperidol or tetrabenazine**.\n- **No staging system** — no Hoehn and Yahr, no UPDRS, no rating scale of any kind.\n- **No prognosis or survival figures** for Parkinson's disease or Huntington's disease.\n- **No non-drug management:** **no physiotherapy and no speech therapy**, beyond deep brain stimulation.\n\nSrc: L3 read end to end; the page audit is a `pdftotext` / `pdffonts` / `pdfimages` sweep of all 51 pages, 2026-08-22. The register rows are quoted from `hem-16` in appdata\theory.neuro.js on disk; the split arithmetic is `content\neuro\theory-plan.md` §4",
