        "h": "Drug-resistant epilepsy — six options beyond drugs",
        "body": "- **⚠️ THE DEFINITION:** **DRUG-RESISTANT EPILEPSY = FAILURE OF TWO OR MORE APPROPRIATE AEDs AT ADEQUATE DOSES.** Both qualifiers matter — **appropriate** for the seizure type (`ep-8`), and **at adequate doses**.\n\n|**Option**|**Detail**|\n|---|---|\n|**⚠️ EPILEPSY SURGERY**|**RESECTION OF THE SEIZURE FOCUS**. **Most effective for TEMPORAL LOBE.** **70 % SEIZURE-FREE POST-OP.** Requires **video-EEG + neuroimaging**|\n|**VAGUS NERVE STIMULATION**|**implanted device**, **stimulates the LEFT VAGUS NERVE**. **~50 % REDUCTION in seizure frequency.** **No cognitive side effects**|\n|**KETOGENIC DIET**|**HIGH FAT, LOW CARBOHYDRATE**. **Effective in CHILDREN.** Mechanism: **altered brain metabolism**. Requires a **specialist dietitian**|\n|**DEEP BRAIN STIMULATION**|**THALAMIC (ANT) stimulation**. **FDA-approved 2018.** For **focal and generalized**. **Adjustable and reversible**|\n|**RESPONSIVE NEUROSTIMULATION**|**DETECTS AND ABORTS seizures**; **focal cortex stimulation**; **learns the patient's EEG patterns**. Requires implantation|\n|**LASER ABLATION (LITT)**|**MR-GUIDED LASER THERAPY**. **Minimally invasive.** **HYPOTHALAMIC HAMARTOMAS.** An **alternative to open surgery**|\n\n- **⚠️ The closing instruction:** it is about **timing, not technique** — **DRUG-RESISTANT? REFER EARLY — epilepsy surgery offers 70 % SEIZURE FREEDOM IN TEMPORAL LOBE EPILEPSY.**\n- *(Deep brain stimulation is also `nr-movement`'s `mv-6` and `mv-10`, for Parkinson's disease and dystonia — **different targets, same technology**: subthalamic and pallidal there, **anterior nucleus of the thalamus** here.)*\n\nSrc: L4 sl. BEYOND AEDs: INTRACTABLE EPILEPSY OPTIONS · KEY CLINICAL TAKEAWAYS (item 05)",
