        "body": "### ⚠️ The split, recorded\n- **Forecast, not found:** `theory-plan.md` §4 named this **the module's only forecast split**, and the old title admitted it — **\"Movement disorders / Epilepsy\"** are **two topics**, not one topic taught over two lectures, so **CLAUDE.md §4's merge rule never applied**.\n- **The seam:** the **deck boundary**. **`L4) Seizures_Epilepsy` here**; **`L3) MOVEMENT DISORDERS` in `nr-movement`**.\n- **The arithmetic:** **2,321 + 2,699 = 5,020 source words**, forecast **15.0 pp at ÷335** and more on every smaller divisor. **`nr-movement` printed 13 pp on its own**, which settles it.\n- **⚠️ Split BEFORE writing** — what the method asks where the evidence is already in hand. **`SCHEDULE` untouched.** **This chapter is new and carries no questions.**\n\n### ⚠️ Register (§14.5) — two rows RECEIVED, both delivered from the deck\n\n|**Owed by**|**Fact**|**Delivered**|\n|---|---|---|\n|**`nr-para`** *(hem-16)*|**EPILEPSY as a disease** — named in `hem-2` only as a tempo cause of hemiplegia|✅ **this chapter entire**|\n|**`nr-para`** *(hem-16)*|**TODD'S PARALYSIS**|✅ **`ep-1`**, in the post-ictal state, and **`ep-3`**, in the recovery row of the syncope checklist. ⚠️ **The deck prints it twice — no fill was needed**|\n\n- **MIGRAINE:** the third name on that row, **already delivered by `nr-headache`** and not repeated.\n- **No row is filed OUT of this chapter.** Every disease named here is either taught here or explicitly handed to a chapter that owns it — see below.\n- **Not repeated:** **stroke and haemorrhage** are `nr-stroke`'s, **meningitis and encephalitis** are `nr-cns`'s. `ep-6` keeps only their **role as seizure causes**.\n\n### ⚠️ Deck quality — the most complete in the module\n- **The page audit:** **32 pages, and NOT ONE carries under 15 extractable words.** No divider slide, no title-art page, no picture-only page anywhere. `pdftotext`, 2026-08-22.\n- **⚠️ Nothing rendered, nothing hidden.** For comparison: `ps-ocd`'s deck had three sparse pages, `nr-movement`'s had six and **one of those could not be read at all**.\n\n### What the deck repeats, written once\n- **The three-step framework** appears **twice** — early, and again as *THE 3-STEP DIAGNOSTIC FRAMEWORK* near the end. Written once, in `ep-2`.\n- **The carbamazepine/phenytoin prohibition** appears **four times** — the AED table, the absence row, the JME case, and the closing takeaways. Written once as a rule in `ep-8` and once inside each case it decides.\n- **The PNES comparison** appears **twice**, as a table in `ep-2` and again inside Fatima's case. The second is kept **as the case's reasoning**, not as a second table.\n\n### What this deck does not contain\n- **⚠️ NO EPIDEMIOLOGY AT ALL.** No prevalence, no incidence, no lifetime risk — for epilepsy, for any seizure type, or for status epilepticus. **`nr-movement` gives figures for Parkinson's disease and Huntington's; this deck gives none for anything.**\n- **⚠️ NO PROGNOSIS**, except the surgical **70 % seizure-free**, the VNS **~50 % reduction** and the ASD-like **50 % of PNES**-adjacent conversion figures. **No remission rate, no relapse rate, no withdrawal-of-therapy guidance.**\n- **⚠️ NO AED SIDE EFFECTS AND NO MONITORING**, beyond **valproate teratogenicity**. Nothing on **phenytoin toxicity, carbamazepine hyponatraemia, lamotrigine rash** or **levetiracetam behavioural effects** — and **no drug levels**.\n- **No DOSE for any maintenance AED** except in the two cases — **ethosuximide and valproate 15-20 mg/kg/day** (Mariam) and **valproate 15-25 mg/kg/day** (Yasin). The status protocol in `ep-10` is the only other place doses appear.\n- **Named and not described:** **LENNOX-GASTAUT syndrome**, **epileptic spasms**, **hypsarrhythmia's syndrome (West)**, **neurocysticercosis**, **anti-NMDAR and LGI1 encephalitis**.\n- **No febrile convulsions as an entity** — fever appears only as a provoking insult and inside the neonatal case.\n- **No counselling topics:** **no driving, employment or pregnancy** guidance, though **job risk** and **contraception** are raised inside two cases.\n- **⚠️ Book Neuro ch.6:** *Epilepsy and Status Epilepticus*, **printed 57-66, ten pages — UNREAD and uncached.** It is the natural first check for any of the gaps above.\n\nSrc: L4 read end to end; the page audit is a `pdftotext` sweep of all 32 pages, 2026-08-22. The register rows are quoted from `hem-16` in appdata\theory.neuro.js on disk; the split arithmetic is `content\neuro\theory-plan.md` §4",
