        "body": "**One skeleton, printed three times:** almost word for word — **exposure provokes IMMEDIATE and MARKED FEAR, OUT OF PROPORTION to the actual danger; 6 MONTHS OR MORE; the patient always AVOIDS; distress and impairment; differentials excluded.** Only the trigger changes.\n\n|**Disorder**|**The trigger**|**⚠️ What is specific to it**|\n|---|---|---|\n|**Specific phobia**|**certain objects** — **animals** (cats) · **environmental** factors (heights) · **blood-injuries** (needles)|the three example families are the book's own, and they are the only sub-typing it gives|\n|**Social anxiety disorder (social phobia)**|**social situations** — **talking or eating in front of others**|**it is performance and observation**, not company as such|\n|**Agoraphobia**|**2 OR MORE** of: public transportation · open spaces · closed places · standing in line or in a crowd · being outside the home alone|**⚠️ the avoidance has a REASON printed** — thoughts that **ESCAPE MIGHT BE DIFFICULT**. And it is the only one of the three with a **threshold count**|\n\n- **⚠️ Agoraphobia is not fear of open spaces.** The list holds **closed places** and **queues** as readily as open ones; what unites them is the escape problem, not the geometry. **A question offering *fear of open spaces* as the definition is testing that.**\n- **⚠️ Two of the three have no letter.** The book's lettering runs **A** generalized anxiety disorder → **B** specific phobia → **(unlettered)** social anxiety disorder → **(unlettered)** panic disorder → **(unlettered)** agoraphobia → **C** OCD → **D** PTSD. **Recorded as printed, not corrected** — the three unlettered headings are in the same blue display face as the lettered ones and are not sub-headings of B.\n\nSrc: neuropsychiatry.pdf (ASM MINDS) Psychiatry ch.3 printed p.195 (specific phobia, social anxiety disorder) and printed p.197 (agoraphobia and its note box). The broken lettering is recorded from the pages themselves",
