        "h": "Differential diagnosis and assessment",
        "body": "### The deck's differential — five limbs, and two of them are its alone\n|**Exclude**|**Example given**|\n|---|---|\n|**⚠️ NORMAL FEAR**|the deck puts it **first**, and the book's list does not contain it at all|\n|**General medical conditions**|—|\n|**Substance induced**|—|\n|**Other types of anxiety disorder**|specific phobia · SAD · panic disorder · agoraphobia|\n|**⚠️ Other disorders WITH an anxiety symptom**|**psychotic disorders** · **DEMENTIA** — the second is the deck's alone|\n\n- **⚠️ They sit at opposite ends:** **normal fear** is the floor — proportionate fear is not a disorder at any duration — and **dementia** is the ceiling, since a newly anxious elderly patient is `ps-geri` and `nr-delirium` territory first.\n- **The book's own four-limb version** — other anxiety disorders, other mental disorders, substance/medication-induced, and another medical condition, with the **fears-insects-because-they-are-advanced-tools** example for psychosis — is written out in **`ps-ocd`'s `oc-6`** and is **not repeated here**. It is printed on the PTSD page but written for the whole category.\n\n### The deck's assessment block\n|**Do**|**In order to establish**|\n|---|---|\n|**History**|the **differential diagnosis**|\n|**Mental state examination**|the **treatment choice and/or follow-up**|\n|**Physical examination**|**associated conditions**|\n|**Investigations**|**medicolegal reasons**|\n\n- **⚠️ Respect somatic c/o.** The deck prints it inside the assessment slide and repeats it on its own *most important pieces of information* slide. It is the same instruction as `ps-symptom`'s **`sy-9`**: a somatic complaint is a **prompt to exclude organicity**, never a reason to stop listening.\n- **⚠️⚠️ NO DIAGNOSTIC TEST.** The deck prints those three words alone, in capitals, at the foot of the assessment slide. **Every investigation in `ax-7` is for exclusion or for the drug — none of them confirms the diagnosis.**\n\nSrc: L4,5 sl. Differential diagnosis · Assessment; the book's four-limb differential from printed p.199 is written in `ps-ocd`'s `oc-6`",
