        "id": "ax-8",
        "w": "must",
        "h": "Which line of treatment — and the rules that govern both",
        "body": "|**Severity**|**What the book prescribes**|\n|---|---|\n|**Mild**|**psychotherapy is the MAIN LINE**|\n|**Moderate and severe**|**a COMBINATION** of psychopharmacological and psychotherapeutic intervention — **better results than pharmacotherapy alone**|\n\n### Psychotherapy — four methods, and a fifth the deck alone names\n- **Printed by the book:** **relaxation techniques** · **systematic desensitization** · **thought stopping technique** · **exposure and response prevention**.\n- **⚠️ The deck names CBT, the book does not:** the deck names **CBT and nothing else**, and the four methods above are the book's, which **never writes the letters CBT** in this chapter — verified, zero hits. **Both recorded, neither corrected.**\n- **⚠️ ERP appears twice, at two scopes:** a **general method** here, and **OCD's specific first-line psychotherapy** in `ps-ocd`'s `oc-8`.\n\n### The rules that govern the drug course\n|**Rule**|**Value**|**Source**|\n|---|---|---|\n|**Onset of clinical improvement**|**2-8 weeks**|**book**|\n|**⚠️ Onset of effect**|**2-6 weeks**|**⚠️ deck — a different number, recorded not reconciled**|\n|**Least duration of treatment**|**12 MONTHS while free of symptoms**; stopping earlier **increases relapse**|book|\n|**Withdrawal**|**one year, then GRADUAL withdrawal** — only the deck says the stop is tapered|deck|\n|**Response rate**|**not all patients respond from the first trial**|deck|\n\n- **⚠️ The OCD figure — 4-12 weeks:** worked in `ps-ocd`'s `oc-8`, and printed here, on this chapter's own spine, as the parenthesis to the 2-8 week rule — so **OCD is the slow one**, and a patient reviewed at six weeks with no response has not failed treatment.\n\n### Three things the patient is told, and one qualification\n- **The intervention is NOT harmful.** · **It DOES NOT mean weakness of personality** — anxiety disorders are **illnesses**. · **It will not cause addiction.**\n- **⚠️ The last one is qualified:** in one source only. The book writes **except for benzodiazepines if used for a prolonged period**; the deck prints **not addictive**, flat. **The book's version is the one to carry**, and it is why the benzodiazepine ceiling in `ax-9` exists.\n\nSrc: neuropsychiatry.pdf (ASM MINDS) Psychiatry ch.3 printed p.200 — Treatment: psychotherapy and psychopharmacology; L4,5 sl. Treatment for the deck's CBT, 2-6 weeks, gradual withdrawal and first-trial lines",
