        "body": "### Indications — both sources print the same ten\n- **Major depressive disorder** · **dysthymia** · **anxiety disorders and OCD** · **eating disorders** · **chronic and neuropathic pain** · **migraine** · **ADHD** · **addiction** · **sleep disorders**.\n- **They may be used ALONE or IN COMBINATION** with other medications. ⚠️ **Only three of the ten are mood disorders** — the *antidepressant is a misnomer* note in `ps-anxiety`'s `ax-9` is this list read from the other end.\n\n### ⚠️⚠️ The six classes — and the DECK NAMES NOT ONE AGENT\n|**Class**|**Agents — all from the BOOK**|\n|---|---|\n|**TCAs** *(tricyclic)*|**amitriptyline · imipramine · clomipramine**|\n|**SSRIs** *(selective serotonin)*|**fluoxetine · paroxetine · sertraline · fluvoxamine · citalopram · escitalopram**|\n|**SNRIs** *(serotonin-noradrenaline)*|**venlafaxine · duloxetine**|\n|**NDRI** *(noradrenaline-dopamine)*|**bupropion**|\n|**NaSSAs** *(noradrenergic and specific serotonergic)*|**mirtazapine**|\n|**MAOIs**|**phenelzine** — printed with a skull, a cheese and a wine glass, and the label ***NOT USED A LOT (TYRAMINE CHEESE REACTION)***|\n\n- **⚠️⚠️ The deck names NO antidepressant:** not one, in 31 slides of psychopharmacology. **All fifteen agents above come from the book's poster**, which is why `ps-pharm` could not be written before that chapter was read.\n- **⚠️ And the two sources classify differently.** The deck's slide 6 gives **FIVE** types — TCAs, SSRIs, SNRIs, **MAOIs**, and **`Atypical Antidepressants`** as one bucket. The book gives **SIX**, splitting that bucket into **NDRI** and **NaSSAs** and naming an agent for each. **The book's is the usable one; both are recorded.**\n- **⚠️ MAOIs are named once — in each source and developed in neither.** The deck lists the class and returns to it never; the book gives it a poster box and **no adverse-effect entry** — see `ph-4`.\n\nSrc: L17 sl.5 (indications) · sl.6 (the pasted `Types of Antidepressants` infographic, watermarked Clarity Clinic); neuropsychiatry.pdf (ASM MINDS) Psychiatry ch.11 printed p.261 — the full-width ANTIDEPRESSANTS poster, read at 300 dpi, which carries all ten indications and all six class boxes",
