        "id": "bp-8",
        "w": "must",
        "h": "Investigations and treatment — and the chapter argues with itself about rest",
        "body": "### Investigations\n|**Setting**|**What is recommended**|\n|---|---|\n|**Uncomplicated mechanical LBP — LABORATORY**|**⚠️ NONE.** *It is recommended that no laboratory investigations be ordered*|\n|**Suspected SYSTEMIC cause** — inflammatory arthritis, connective tissue disease, infection|**CBC, ESR** and other markers may be appropriate|\n|**ACUTE mechanical LBP, no red flags — IMAGING**|**⚠️ NONE.** ⚠️ *(the deck adds a qualifier the book does not print: **patients between 20 and 50 years old** with no red flags do not require imaging)*|\n|**CHRONIC low back pain**|**AP and lateral lumbosacral X-rays** may be appropriate|\n|**Pain radiating BELOW THE KNEES**|**MRI may be indicated**|\n\n- **⚠️ What imaging cannot do:** it **can CONFIRM a clinical diagnosis but CANNOT confirm that a particular structure is the cause of the pain.** The book prints that sentence deliberately, and it is the answer to *why not scan everyone*.\n- **⚠️ The age qualifier:** it is **red flag 1 restated** (`bp-1`) — under 20 or over 50 is itself a red flag, so *20 to 50 with no red flags* is not an extra rule — it is the same rule twice.\n\n### Treatment of low back pain and sciatica\n- **⚠️ Conservative treatment is — for patients WITHOUT any neurological deficit**, and it is **usually applied for 4-6 WEEKS**.\n- **It includes:** **bed rest for 2-4 DAYS on a hard board mattress** · activity modification and **avoiding heavy lifting** · **analgesics and NSAIDs** · **muscle relaxants** · **reduction of body weight** · **external lumbar support** · **physical therapy**.\n\n### Treatment specific to disc prolapse\n- **Conservative:** **INTERMITTENT bed rest** with movement for short periods in between · a **firm mattress**, in the most comfortable position · a **RIGID LUMBAR ORTHOSIS**, which **can shorten the duration of bed rest or obviate the need for it** · **heat/cold application**.\n- **Analgesics and anti-inflammatory drugs:** ⚠️ **the heading names NO drug and NO dose.** In **hyperalgic** forms, **intrathecal injection of steroids by LUCHERINI'S TECHNIQUE** can produce a remarkable reduction in pain; **epidural analgesia** in severe cases.\n- **Surgery:** indicated on **failure of conservative management** or **when a neurological deficit is present** — **chemonucleolysis**, **percutaneous discectomy**.\n- **⚠️ `Rehabilitation`:** a heading **whose entire body is two words** — ***Therapeutic Exercises.***\n\n### Surgical indications for low back pain and sciatica\n|**Relative**|**⚠️ ABSOLUTE**|\n|---|---|\n|**failure of conservative measures**|**CAUDA EQUINA SYNDROME** · **progressive or persistent neurological MOTOR deficit** · **severe, unremitting LEG PAIN** not relieved by conservative measures · the presence of a **visceral complaint** · **pain not responding to medical therapy**|\n\n- **⚠️ The surgical section names NO PROCEDURE.** The lumbar procedures are the two on the disc-prolapse page above. **Read the two treatment blocks together; neither is complete alone.**\n\n### ⚠️⚠️ THREE STATEMENTS ABOUT REST, AND THEY DO NOT AGREE\n|**Where**|**What it says**|\n|---|---|\n|printed **158** (`bp-2`)|the goal for **both acute and chronic** back pain is **to be ACTIVE AS SOON AS POSSIBLE**|\n|printed **163**|**INTERMITTENT bed rest**, no duration; and an **orthosis can obviate the need for it**|\n|printed **165**|**BED REST FOR 2-4 DAYS** on a hard board mattress|\n\n- **All three are recorded — and NONE is reconciled.** They are not flatly contradictory — 2-4 days is short — but **a question asking *how long should this patient rest* has three printed answers in one chapter.** **Quote the page the question comes from.**\n\nSrc: neuropsychiatry.pdf (ASM MINDS) Neurology ch.16 printed p.163 (disc-prolapse Treatment and Rehabilitation) and printed p.165 (Investigations, Treatment, Surgical indications); the rest contradiction is against printed p.158. L11 sl. Investigations · Treatment — which prints the conservative block TWICE, on two consecutive slides, and adds the 20-to-50 age qualifier",
