        "id": "np-6",
        "w": "must",
        "h": "The twelve specific tests",
        "body": "|**Test**|**For**|**How**|\n|---|---|---|\n|**Adson's test**|**CERVICAL RIB**|deep breath, **head turned TOWARD the side of the lesion**; watch for **radial pulse obliteration** or decrease|\n|**Lateral stretch test**|**radiculopathy**|**stretch the neck in the OPPOSITE direction** — elicits pain along the nerve root distribution|\n|**⚠️ Lhermitte's test**|**MYELOPATHY** — spinal canal stenosis, **multiple sclerosis**, cervical disc impingement, tumour|an **ELECTRIC SHOCK SENSATION** on **NECK FLEXION**, often radiating down the spine|\n|**Rust's sign**|**severe SPRAIN or SUBLUXATION**|the patient **holds the weight of the head in the hands**, or lifts the head manually when arising from lying down|\n|**⚠️ Ankle clonus**|**UMN LESION**|quickly **dorsiflex the foot** while cradling the heel to relieve the load|\n|**Bakody sign**|**cervical radiculopathy**, typically **C4-C6**|the patient **raises the hand ONTO THE TOP OF THE HEAD**; **reduction or elimination of radicular pain is positive** and suggests root compression|\n|**Compression**|nerve root tension / radiculopathy|seated, **press DOWNWARD on top of the skull**|\n|**Distraction**|nerve root tension / radiculopathy|**pull UPWARD on the skull**|\n|**Doorbell sign**|nerve root tension / radiculopathy|**deep palpation of C5**|\n|**Halstead manoeuvre**|**NEUROVASCULAR COMPRESSION**|seated, palpate the radial pulse, then **pull traction on the arm downward** while the patient **extends the head backward**|\n|**⚠️ Hoffmann's sign**|**MYELOPATHIC sign**|**flick the DIP joint of the long finger**; observe **reflex flexion of the IP joint of index and thumb**|\n|**Jackson's compression**|**nerve compression**|seated, the patient **bends the head obliquely BACKWARD**; then apply **downward pressure on the head**|\n\n- **⚠️ Three of the twelve test the CORD — not the root:** **Lhermitte's**, **Hoffmann's** and **ankle clonus**. **Everything else is a root or a vascular test.** **That grouping is not printed; it is the useful way to hold twelve names.**\n- **⚠️ Compression — and distraction are the same test in reverse** — press down to reproduce, pull up to relieve. **Bakody is the third of the same family**, relieving radicular pain by taking tension off the root.\n- **⚠️ Ankle clonus, in a cervical table:** a **lower-limb sign**, with **no explanation of why**. **Recorded as printed** — and the reason is that cervical **myelopathy** produces long-tract signs below the lesion, which is `np-2`'s group c. *(The connection is supplied.)*\n- **⚠️ Hoffmann's caption prints `Flip` — in the drawing and `Flick` in the bullet.** **Both recorded.**\n\nSrc: neuropsychiatry.pdf (ASM MINDS) Neurology ch.16 printed pp. 170-171 — `Specific Tests:`, a two-column table that **SPANS THE PAGE BREAK**: eight tests on 170 and four on 171, with no repeated heading. The cord/root grouping and the ankle-clonus explanation are supplied per `CLAUDE.md` §4",
